.TH HERCULES 1 "November 2026" "Hercules 4.x" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hercules \\- IBM System/370, ESA/390 and z/Architecture emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hercules
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ configuration-file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hercules
emulates IBM System/370, ESA/390 and 64-bit z/Architecture mainframe hardware.
It provides emulated processors, main storage, channel subsystems and
peripheral devices so that compatible mainframe operating systems and
applications can run on a Linux host.
.PP
Hercules is normally started with a configuration file describing the
machine model, storage size, devices and network interfaces. The emulator
provides an interactive operator console for controlling the emulated
machine.
.SH OPTIONS
The available command-line options depend on the upstream Hercules build.
Run
.B hercules -h
or consult the installed Hercules documentation for the complete list.
.PP
A configuration file may be supplied as the final argument. If omitted,
Hercules uses its default configuration behavior and may prompt for required
configuration information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hercules/
System-wide location reserved for Hercules configuration files.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hercules/
Installed Hercules data and documentation files.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hercules/
Suggested location for persistent emulator data, disk images and tapes.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start Hercules with a configuration file:
.PP
.nf
hercules /etc/hercules/my-system.cnf
.fi
.PP
Display command-line help:
.PP
.nf
hercules -h
.fi
.SH NOTES
The emulator does not include IBM operating system software, licensed
mainframe programs, disk images or other proprietary guest materials.
Those must be obtained and used under their respective licenses.
.PP
Network devices, tun/tap networking and privileged host-device access may
require additional host configuration and permissions. Do not run the
emulator with elevated privileges unless the selected device configuration
requires it and the security implications are understood.
.SH SEE ALSO
